    "result_text": "The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented membership level 4 gated on tenure of more than 365 days.\n\n**Design** \u2014 I mirrored the existing `AgeBand` pattern, where the date-derivation util takes an explicit \"as of\" reference date and callers supply it, rather than reaching for `LocalDate.now()` inside the pure logic. This keeps the level calculation deterministic and testable.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- `util/MembershipLevels.java` \u2014 Added tenure as a fourth qualifying factor alongside email and no-namesake. `of(Owner, LocalDate asOf)` now adds a point when `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, asOf) > TENURE_DAYS` (365), raising `MAX` from 3 to 4. Tenure logic lives in a small private `hasTenure` helper (null-safe on registration date). Because the three pre-tenure factors cap at 3, level 4 is reachable *only* with the tenure point \u2014 so tenure is a genuine requirement for level 4, and a new owner (zero tenure) never exceeds 3.\n\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `membershipLevel` now passes `LocalDate.now()` as the reference date.\n\n- `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 Updated the audit call to the new signature (creation time = current date).\n\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 Updated the `membershipLevel` schema description and `maximum` (3 \u2192 4) to match.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` confirms a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 lands at level 3, not 4.",
